Last game I had a pet that turned into a lich, and promoted itself
through it's own hard work to eventually become an arch-lich with 296
HP.  Good news with them is that they don't eat your corpses, they
like to teleport next to you, and to susceptible monsters they are
absolutely deadly.  I suppose this is why people genocide them.  It
could take out shopkeepers in two turns.  The bad news is that they
don't eat, they teleport in front of you which is annoying sometimes.

They have a habit of choosing attacks that have no effect on the
intended targets.  It would cover blue jellies and other things with
frost.  Mine had this habit of 'touching' the priest.  The priest
would not lose any hit points, but the priest didn't like it.  This is
a real problem if your reason for having a tough pet is to mow down
priests for their swag.

